sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: MPP charge with the stripe method (Shared Payment Token)
  accDescr: Sequence diagram: MPP charge with the stripe method (Shared Payment Token). 4 participants: Client (agent), Stripe (client account), Seller server, and Stripe (seller account). 6 steps, 6 crossing a trust boundary, 2 failure branches. Based on stripe-mpp draft-stripe-charge-00 (undated, repository text of 2026-09-09, unchanged at commit 50309c8) (2026-09-09). Step 1: Seller server to Client (agent): 402 with method= stripe. This step crosses a trust boundary. Step 2: Client (agent) to Stripe (client account): Create a Shared Payment Token. This step crosses a trust boundary. Step 3: Client (agent) to Seller server: Retry with credential payload spt. This step crosses a trust boundary. Step 4: Seller server to Stripe (seller account): Create PaymentIntent (confirm true). This step crosses a trust boundary. If The same credential is sent again: same challenge id and SPT, so the same idempotency key, and Stripe returns the earlier PaymentIntent with Idempotent-Replayed: true: Reject it as a replay. mppx before 0.4.11 counted it as a new payment (CVE-2026-34210) the draft also requires single-use challenge ids. Step 5: Stripe (seller account) to Seller server: PaymentIntent status. This step crosses a trust boundary. If Any other status: 402 with a fresh challenge. Step 6: Seller server to Client (agent): 200 with Payment-Receipt. This step crosses a trust boundary.
  autonumber
  participant p_client as Client (agent)
  participant p_stripe as Stripe (client account)
  participant p_server as Seller server
  participant p_stripeS as Stripe (seller account)
  p_server-->>p_client: 402 with method=#quot;stripe#quot;
  Note over p_server,p_client: Crosses a trust boundary
  p_client->>p_stripe: Create a Shared Payment Token
  Note over p_client,p_stripe: Crosses a trust boundary
  p_client->>p_server: Retry with credential payload #123;spt#125;
  Note over p_client,p_server: Crosses a trust boundary
  alt Expected path
    p_server->>p_stripeS: Create PaymentIntent (confirm true)
    Note over p_server,p_stripeS: Crosses a trust boundary
  else The same credential is sent again: same challenge id and SPT, so the same idempotency key, and Stripe returns the earlier PaymentIntent with Idempotent-Replayed: true
    Note over p_server,p_stripeS: Reject it as a replay. mppx before 0.4.11 counted<br/>it as a new payment (CVE-2026-34210)#59; the draft<br/>also requires single-use challenge ids.
  end
  alt Expected path
    p_stripeS-->>p_server: PaymentIntent status
    Note over p_stripeS,p_server: Crosses a trust boundary
  else Any other status
    Note over p_stripeS,p_server: 402 with a fresh challenge.
  end
  p_server-->>p_client: 200 with Payment-Receipt
  Note over p_server,p_client: Crosses a trust boundary
